{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Assemble</b> — Gather together, from the root עיש, which is seven stars that never separate, for they are in the upper sphere and are visible in summer and winter on earth." "<b>Come down</b> — Like הורד, and these are the words of the prophet, and the meaning is that HaShem brought [them] down." "<b>Your warriors</b> — [Is] a divine name, and they are the angels, corresponding to 'he aroused the warriors,' and this word is well known in the Targum, and likewise נחת גדודיה על עפר נחת. And Yefet said: 'There HaShem will break your warriors, you the enemy who come,' like ונחתה קשת נחושת."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:44.892926576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}